FAILURE MECHANISMS — ROOT CAUSE MAP

FM-01 "Vknee Blindspot"
  Root cause: pa_lineup_canvas.js::calculateOptimalImpedance() omits Vknee
  Effect chain: wrong Ropt → wrong Zt (combiner) → wrong match element values
               → transistor 5.1 sees inconsistent impedance target from canvas
  Fix: Ropt = (Vdd - Vknee)² / (2 × Pout); Vknee from technology_guardrails.yaml

FM-02 "Doherty Polarity Flip"  
  Root cause: calc_pa_lineup.R backoff PAE model (pout_ratio^0.8) is for
              conventional class-AB. Doherty has load modulation that maintains
              efficiency at backoff — using class-AB model actually predicts
              worsening efficiency exactly where Doherty improves it.
  Effect chain: backoff PAE shown as degrading → wrong Idq bias calc in 5.1
               → wrong thermal calc → false reliability prediction
  Correct Doherty efficiency at backoff:
    η_doherty(p) = η_peak × √(p/p_max)   [for p ≤ p_max/2, main PA only]
    η_doherty(p) = η_peak                  [at p_max, both PAs saturated]
    At 6dB OBO (p = p_max/4): η = η_peak × 0.5 / ideal, but maintained above class-AB

FM-03 "Three-Oracle Problem"
  Root cause: technology selection decided independently in 3 places
  Effect chain: spec tab shows tech from R (recommend_technology),
               canvas shows tech from JS (selectTechnology),
               guardrails validation checks against YAML
               → at boundary regions (e.g. 2 GHz, 50W GaN vs LDMOS)
               all three can give different answers for the same operating point
  Fix: YAML is the oracle; JS and R both parse the guardrails at startup
       and build their decision trees from YAML data

FM-04 "Series Doherty"
  Root cause: distributeGain() creates [Driver → PA] stages in series for Doherty
              topology, where the PA stage gain represents only one branch
  Effect chain: cascade shows single PA gain; actual Doherty has main+peak PAs
              in parallel each with gain = spec_gain - driver_gain;
              the gain model implies series amplification instead of
              parallel combining — fundamentally wrong topology representation
  Fix: for Doherty, gain distribution must be:
       - Driver chain (series): gains up to the splitter
       - Main PA: remaining gain (one branch)
       - Peak PA: same gain as main PA (one branch, parallel)
       - Both are combined by the Doherty combiner

FM-05 "Vdd Phantom Power"
  Root cause: spec_supply_voltage default = 30V instead of 28V
  Effect chain: Ropt = (30)²/(2P) vs correct (28-Vknee)²/(2P)
              at 55.3 dBm, Vknee=2: correct=(26)²/2×679=0.499Ω
              with bug=(30)²/2×679=0.662Ω (33% error on PA stage)
  Fix: default Vdd = 28V, pull from technology_guardrails.yaml::GaN_SiC::vdd::typical
  
